-- title:
--   Extending a DVR along a finitely generated field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, and let $s$ be a finite subset of $L$ which generates $L$ over $K$, in the sense that the intermediate field generated by $K$ and $s$ inside $L$ is all of $L$ ($\mathrm{adjoin}\,K\,s = \top$). Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ whose underlying ring is a discrete valuation ring. Then there exists a valuation subring $V$ of $L$ such that: the underlying ring of $V$ is a discrete valuation ring; every $x \in K$ lying in $W$ has image $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,L\,x$ lying in $V$; and every $x \in W$ lying in the maximal ideal of the local ring $W$ has image in `V.nonunits`, the set of elements of $L$ whose $V$-valuation is $<1$, that is, the maximal ideal of $V$ viewed inside $L$. In other words, $V$ is a discretely valued valuation subring of $L$ dominating $W$ along the structure map $K \to L$. No algebraicity or finiteness of the degree $[L:K]$ is assumed, only that $L$ is generated over $K$ by finitely many elements.
--
--   This is the statement that a discrete valuation ring of a field extends, as a dominating discrete valuation ring, to any finitely generated extension field; finite generation is essential, since over an algebraic extension of infinite degree a discrete valuation need not extend discretely. It is the input to the discrete valuative criterion of integrality over a Noetherian base, [`Algebra.IsIntegral.of_forall_valuationSubring_isDiscreteValuationRing_apply_mem`](thm.html#Algebra.IsIntegral.of_forall_valuationSubring_isDiscreteValuationRing_apply_mem). The proof reduces to the two one-generator cases already available: the finite-degree case [`ValuationSubring.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_dominates_of_finiteDimensional`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_dominates_of_finiteDimensional) (Krull–Akizuki) and the purely transcendental case [`ValuationSubring.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_dominates_of_transcendental_of_adjoin_eq_top`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_dominates_of_transcendental_of_adjoin_eq_top) (Gauss valuation).
-- source:
